{"id":"FIG-a585e9e921b605ba","src":"figure","doc":"AUTOSAR_SWS_OS","page":42,"text":"","caption":"Figure 7.4: States of an implicit synchronized schedule table 2. explicit synchronization – the schedule table is driven by an OS counter which is not the counter with which synchronization is required. The OS provides additional functionality to keep schedule table processing driven by the OS counter synchronized with the synchronization counter. This is typically how synchronization with broadcast periodically global times works. The next figure shows the states of such schedule tables.","sha":"a585e9e921b605ba7f7c5c92d0e53a7e1f7fd80be5e55e52f05764b9f70c9a8f","series":[{"id":"FIG-a585e9e921b605ba","releases":["R3.0.7","R3.1.5","R3.2.3"],"sha":"a585e9e921b605ba7f7c5c92d0e53a7e1f7fd80be5e55e52f05764b9f70c9a8f"}],"releases":["R3.0.7","R3.1.5","R3.2.3"],"occurrences":[{"release":"R3.0.7","doc":"AUTOSAR_SWS_OS","page":42,"pdf":"R3.0.7/AUTOSAR/CLASSIC/AUTOSAR_SWS_OS.pdf"},{"release":"R3.1.5","doc":"AUTOSAR_SWS_OS","page":42,"pdf":"R3.1.5/AUTOSAR/CLASSIC/AUTOSAR_SWS_OS.pdf"}],"kind":"figure","platform":"classic","targets":[{"role":"heuristic","conf":0.9,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"Defines ScheduleTableStatusType enumeration values","rel":[],"id":"SWS_Os_00784"},{"role":"heuristic","conf":0.85,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"NextScheduleTable transitions between schedule tables","rel":[],"id":"SWS_Os_00191"},{"role":"heuristic","conf":0.85,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"StartScheduleTableAbs starts schedule table","rel":[],"id":"SWS_Os_00351"},{"role":"heuristic","conf":0.8,"rt":"","m":"gemini-3.8-flash","why":"ScheduleTableType identifier definition","rel":[],"id":"SWS_Os_00783"}],"ok":true,"schema":"versions-explorer@1"}